# Per-project route files stay on the box and out of this public repo.
#
# Traefik watches this whole directory, so a project can drop its own routes in
# here - often generated by that project's tooling - and they take effect at
# once. Those files name private work and change without this repo knowing, so
# the default is: NOT tracked.
#
# Deny everything, then allow back the files that genuinely belong to the stack.
# A new project file is therefore ignored automatically, which is the safe way
# round: forgetting to add an ignore rule cannot leak anything.
*
!.gitignore
!auth.yml
!host-services.yml
!bothy-api.yml
!project.example.yml
# THE ROLE GATES - the only definitions of sso-viewer, sso-editor and
# sso-operator, referenced by every tier file below (2026-09). The most
# load-bearing file in this directory: without it every gated router errors. No
# credential - a role name is not a secret. Added in the same commit as the file,
# because of every note below.
!bothy-gates.yml
# The file-explorer routes. Stack-owned and load-bearing: its role gates are the
# ONLY thing standing between the tailnet and write access to the repos. It
# contains no credential, and losing it would silently remove the editor tier's
# routes, so it is tracked. It was ignored by the `*` above for its first two
# commits, which is exactly the failure mode this comment exists to prevent
# repeating. (It defined sso-viewer/sso-editor itself until 2026-09.)
!bothy-files.yml
# The config-form routes, tracked for exactly the reason bothy-files.yml is:
# they put the `editor` gate on a path that can rewrite this repo's compose
# files. It holds no credential. Served by bothy-files since 2026-09.
!bothy-config.yml
# The action routes: container verbs and cluster actions (bothy-ops). Tracked
# for the strongest reason of all - the operator gate on the one service that can
# stop this box's databases. Replaces bothy-control.yml and bothy-kube.yml
# (2026-09), both of which were allow-listed here and are deleted: a stale
# `!name` line for a file that no longer exists would let a hand-made file of
# that name be committed without anyone reading this list. bothy-kube.yml was
# written in a worktree, IGNORED by the `*` above, and missed its first merge
# (2026-09-17) - which is why this line went in with the file.
!bothy-ops.yml
# The redacted twin of the GENERATED bothy-prom.yml (which stays ignored by the
# `*` above - it carries a basic-auth credential). Comments only: a live example
# in this directory overwrites the real router, see the file's own header.
!bothy-prom.example.yml
# The Settings admin reads (bothy-ops admin.py): users, credentials inventory,
# backups, audit log - four exact Path() GET routers behind sso-operator.
# HAND-WRITTEN and separate from bothy-ops.yml, whose kube routers are generated.
# No credential. Allow-listed in the same commit as the file, for the reason
# every entry above gives.
!bothy-admin.yml
